</p>

<section id="download" class="section-block">
	<h2>1. Download</h2>
	<p>Choose the build that suits your deployment. If you're unsure, use the <strong>installer (.exe)</strong>.</p>
	{% include "partials/phone-desktop-downloads.njk" %}
</section>

<section id="verify" class="section-block">
	<h2>2. Verify checksum (optional)</h2>
	<p>Validate file integrity by comparing SHA-256 checksums.</p>
	<ol>
		<li>Open <strong>Windows PowerShell</strong>.</li>
		<li>Run: <code>Get-FileHash .\VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}-Setup.exe -Algorithm SHA256</code></li>
		<li>Compare the output with the value listed above.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section id="install" class="section-block">
	<h2>3. Install</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Double-click the downloaded <strong>-Setup.exe</strong> file. For the portable build, run the <strong>.exe</strong> directly, or extract the <strong>.zip</strong> and run the app inside it.</li>
		<li>If Windows SmartScreen appears, click <em>More info</em>, then <em>Run anyway</em>.</li>
		<li>Follow the installation wizard to complete setup.</li>
	</ol>
	<p><strong>Upgrading?</strong> Fully quit the running app from the system tray (right-click &rarr; <em>Quit</em>) before installing; otherwise the single-instance lock re-focuses the old version.</p>
</section>

<section id="firstlaunch" class="section-block">
	<h2>4. First launch</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>Open <strong>VoiceTel</strong> (or <strong>VoiceML Phone</strong>) from the Start Menu.</li>
		<li>Allow microphone access when prompted. If you missed the prompt, go to <em>Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; security &rarr; Microphone</em>, enable <em>Microphone access</em>, and allow the app.</li>
		<li>Enter your VoiceTel SIP credentials (username, password, display name) as provisioned in the customer portal. In VoiceML Phone, enter your VoiceML activation code under <em>Settings &rarr; Auto Provision</em> instead.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section id="faq" class="section-block faq-block">
	<h2>FAQ</h2>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>How do I uninstall or repair the app?</summary>
		<p>Open <em>Settings &rarr; Apps &rarr; Installed apps</em>. Locate <strong>VoiceTel</strong> and choose <em>Uninstall</em> or <em>Modify/Repair</em> if available.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>What if audio doesn't work?</summary>
		<p>Check input/output devices in Windows Sound settings and verify microphone permissions are enabled.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>Where can I find logs?</summary>
		<p>Logs are stored in <code>%APPDATA%\VoiceTelPhone\logs</code>. You can share them with support if needed.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>Why does the installer request admin rights?</summary>
		<p>Admin privileges are required to register audio components and add VoiceTel Phone to the Start Menu.</p>
	</details>
	<details class="faq-item">
		<summary>Can I install without admin rights?</summary>
		<p>Yes — use the portable executable (.exe) or the .zip archive above.</p>
	</details>
</section>

